Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nProbibility eXt, short for Existence for us in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", equtons, is 50%. Has only two states: True or False. Count 1 or zero\n\n\
False = null, undefined, having no properties, observable or unobservable, \
Count = zero. What the \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] is, if \
anything, I auguer is that is \[OpenCurlyQuote]nothing\[CloseCurlyQuote] not \
even potentual energy. It sums to \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] \
there is no zero placeholder. Leave for thouse smarter then me to work out. \
That the summation for the \[OpenCurlyQuote]Universe\[CloseCurlyQuote] must \
be \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] is a premis of this model; as is \
the null state and eXt state exist in supperposition, both states are present \
in any measurment. At base level count 1 there is no way to tell them apart \
as neither has obserable properities. \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] \
as it has none, eXt as there is no reference against which it can be \
comparied thus its properties are unobserable.\n\nTrue =  eXt = Unity = 1, \
Count = 1. There is a count it is equal to one. It is one dimentionl. It is \
unobservable directly as thene is no reference, a reference requires a count \
of 2. \n\n"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.5125978593125*^9, {3.51259789903125*^9, 3.5125980849375*^9}, {
   3.512598116375*^9, 3.51259812078125*^9}, {3.512598194234375*^9, 
   3.5125983486875*^9}, {3.512598383375*^9, 3.512598438734375*^9}, 
   3.512598572015625*^9, {3.51259861346875*^9, 3.512598691078125*^9}, {
   3.512598924734375*^9, 3.5125989274375*^9}, {3.51259901421875*^9, 
   3.512599238625*^9}, {3.512706044640625*^9, 3.5127060615625*^9}, {
   3.51270611084375*^9, 3.512706152890625*^9}}],

