Cell["\<\
Assumtion: eXt properity exist as a pair properity. There is the properity of \
Exitance measured against the reference of where the existance is \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote]. The \[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] reflects the requiremmt that the \[OpenCurlyQuote]Sum\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] of the Universe = \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote]

The \[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote] is given a value of \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]reflective\[CloseCurlyQuote] (-) with a Count = 1, it is the \
recriprical value of eXt without the properity of Existence, it is the \
Shaddow of Existnce cast on the \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] It is \
a \[OpenCurlyQuote]Hole\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] left in \[OpenCurlyQuote]Null\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] when eXt properity is present. The \[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] has no properities, it is the abcensts of a properity \
analogious to Holes in semiconductors.

Given the eXt properity there will be the shaddow properity of \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote] It will seem to behave as if it had \
all the peropritys of eXt  reflectivily. 

The \[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote] is the hole left in the \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] when the eXt property is present, it \
is the shaddow that eXt cast on the \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote], \
the place where the eXt \[OpenCurlyQuote]energy\[CloseCurlyQuote] is not.

There is either \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\[CloseCurlyQuote] or {eXt \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote]} pair. eXt without \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote] same as \[OpenCurlyQuote]null\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] <eXt|Not>, <1|-1>, <1| - | -1>

The {eXt \[OpenCurlyQuote]Not\[CloseCurlyQuote]} pair has physical reality; \
actully is the 1st step in defining or creating physical observed reality.

eXt is a pure Complex entity.




\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.512706216984375*^9, 3.5127065175*^9}, {
  3.512706600203125*^9, 3.5127066019375*^9}, {3.512706753046875*^9, 
  3.51270687590625*^9}, {3.5127069076875*^9, 3.512706961140625*^9}, {
  3.51270702534375*^9, 3.512707099265625*^9}, {3.512707185609375*^9, 
  3.512707198625*^9}, {3.5127072496875*^9, 3.51270746634375*^9}, {
  3.51270925153125*^9, 3.5127093609375*^9}, {3.5127099886875*^9, 
  3.51271011178125*^9}, {3.51271017803125*^9, 3.512710265484375*^9}, {
  3.512710297859375*^9, 3.512710353734375*^9}, {3.512715282625*^9, 
  3.51271534915625*^9}, {3.512715783265625*^9, 3.5127158038125*^9}, {
  3.512716221546875*^9, 3.51271623015625*^9}, {3.512777026265625*^9, 
  3.51277708496875*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Based on equ 5.2.5 of \[OpenCurlyQuote]The Power Of \
Alpha\[CloseCurlyQuote](TPOA) by Malcolm H.MacGregoras the model 

The potentual energy of eXt-\[OpenCurlyQuote]not\[CloseCurlyQuote] pair is \
PtEgr === (eXt^2)/2r

r is the speration distance, value to be determend but assumed for now as \
either 1 or Pi

\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.512779141359375*^9, 3.51277915321875*^9}, 
   3.51277918403125*^9, {3.51277922840625*^9, 3.512779343921875*^9}, {
   3.512833157140625*^9, 3.5128331811875*^9}, {3.512841244515625*^9, 
   3.51284127484375*^9}, {3.512841404765625*^9, 3.512841493546875*^9}, {
   3.512842018234375*^9, 3.5128420184375*^9}, {3.51284207803125*^9, 
   3.51284218609375*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"eXt", "^", "2"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"r", "=", "1"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"eXt", "^", "2"}], ")"}], "/", " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "r"}], ")"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"r", "=", "Pi"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"eXt", "^", "2"}], ")"}], "/", " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"2", "r"}], ")"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.51284156571875*^9, 3.512841573875*^9}, {
  3.512842189078125*^9, 3.5128422534375*^9}, {3.51284257275*^9, 
